title: To the Masses
subtitle: The Third Congress of the Communist International judges the German party.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 7 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and e21_third_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_third_done = 1;
Q.e21_lenin_mood = (Q.ecci_lenin >= 60) ? 1 : ((Q.ecci_lenin >= 40) ? 2 : 3);
// Levi's chances, if his case is still open, before anyone pleads for him
var p = 20 + (Q.independence - 50) / 2 + 2 * ((Q.history_luxemburgist || 0) - (Q.history_offensive || 0)) + (Q.ecci_lenin - 50) / 2;
if (Q.luxemburg_alive == 1) { p += 20; }
Q.e21_plea_p = Math.max(5, Math.min(75, p + 30));
Q.e21_plea_odds = (Q.e21_plea_p < 35) ? 1 : ((Q.e21_plea_p < 60) ? 2 : 3);
Q.e21_levi_open = (Q.e21_levi_fate == 2 && Q.levi_in_party == 1) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.comintern_member == 1) {
    RG.directive({
        id: 'masses',
        title: 'To the masses!',
        text: 'The Third World Congress instructs every section to win the majority of the working class before it calls on it to fight for power: in the factories, in the unions and by the united front.',
        from: 'lenin',
        months: 5,
        goals: [{q: 'worker_support', op: '>=', v: Math.min(75, Math.round(Q.worker_support + 6))},
                {q: 'spd_relation', op: '>=', v: Math.min(60, Math.round(Q.spd_relation + 8))}],
        reward: {subsidy: 1, faction: 'unionist'},
        punish: 'rebuke',
        announce: false
    });
}
!}

= To the Masses

The Third Congress of the International sits in the Kremlin from 22 June to 12 July, and the German question takes more of its time than any other.

[? if march_action = 1 : Zinoviev and Bukharin defend the March Action as a step forward. Lenin says that the theory of the offensive is nonsense, and that a party which has not won the majority of the working class cannot take power for it. ?][? if march_action = 0 : Zinoviev and Kun accuse the German Zentrale of letting Hörsing take Mansfeld without a fight. Lenin cuts them short: a party that has not won the majority must not be provoked into fighting for it. ?][? if march_action = 2 : Zinoviev hails the victory in Central Germany. Lenin says that one district is not Germany, and that the party must now win the majority of the working class. ?] His slogan for the congress is: to the masses!

[? if e21_lenin_mood = 1 : Lenin's anger is for Kun and the emissaries, and he speaks of the German comrades as people who can be trusted to learn. ?][? if e21_lenin_mood = 2 : Lenin is not hostile to the German delegation, and not patient with it either. ?][? if e21_lenin_mood = 3 : Lenin names the German Zentrale in his speech, and not kindly. ?][? if e21_levi_open = 1 : Levi's case is on the agenda, and Zetkin has come to plead for him. ?][? if e21_levi_fate = 1 : Zetkin has come to plead for Levi, who has been expelled. ?]

- @accept: Accept the theses.
- @defend: Defend the March Action.
- @promise: Promise that next time we will fight.
- @plea: Plead for Levi with Lenin.
- @own: Accept the theses, and say we will apply them our own way.

@accept
subtitle: Lenin, Trotsky and Radek will be pleased. The word "offensive" leaves the Rote Fahne.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_masses_stance = 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.comply(35);
RG.ecci('lenin', 8);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 6);
!}
go-to: verdict

@defend
view-if: march_action != 0 and offensive_gone = 0
subtitle: Zinoviev will be grateful. Lenin will remember.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_masses_stance = 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
RG.ecci('lenin', -10);
!}
go-to: verdict

@promise
view-if: march_action = 0 and offensive_gone = 0
subtitle: Zinoviev applauds. Lenin asks who will do the fighting.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_masses_stance = 2;
Q.militancy += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 5);
RG.ecci('lenin', -5);
!}
go-to: verdict

@plea
view-if: e21_levi_open = 1 or e21_levi_fate = 1
subtitle: [? if e21_levi_fate = 1 : Levi is out. Lenin might leave the door open for him to come back. ?][? if e21_levi_open = 1 and e21_plea_odds = 1 : Zetkin does not think Lenin can be moved. ?][? if e21_levi_open = 1 and e21_plea_odds = 2 : Zetkin thinks Lenin might go either way. ?][? if e21_levi_open = 1 and e21_plea_odds = 3 : Zetkin thinks Lenin will listen. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_plea = 1;
Q.e21_masses_stance = 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
!}
go-to: verdict

@own
subtitle: A declaration of independence, made politely. Moscow's money will be shorter.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_masses_stance = 4;
Q.independence += 8;
Q.moscow_subsidy = Math.max(0, Q.moscow_subsidy - 1);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -8);
RG.ecci('radek', 2);
!}
go-to: verdict

@verdict
title: The Verdict
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_verdict = 0;
if (Q.e21_levi_open == 1) {
    var p = Q.e21_levi_plea ? Q.e21_plea_p : Math.max(5, Q.e21_plea_p - 30);
    if (100 * Math.random() < p) {
        Q.e21_levi_verdict = 2;
        Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
        RG.news('Lenin saves Levi: censured, not expelled', 2);
    } else {
        Q.e21_levi_verdict = 1;
        Q.e21_levi_fate = 1;
        RG.expel('levi', {news: 'The world congress expels Paul Levi', priority: 3});
        Q.levi_in_party = 0;
        Q.levi_split = 1;
        Q.levi_advisor = 0;
        var heir = (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') ? 'unionist' : Q.leading_faction;
        for (var d of Q.districts) {
            Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.9;
            if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'luxemburgist') {
                Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.7;
                Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = heir;
                Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 45;
            }
        }
        if (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') {
            Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
            Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
        }
        Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 15;
    }
} else if (Q.e21_levi_fate == 1) {
    Q.e21_levi_verdict = 3;
}
!}

[? if e21_masses_stance = 1 : The German delegation votes for the theses on tactics without amendment. ?][? if e21_masses_stance = 2 : The Berlin delegates defend every day of March, and Lenin makes them rewrite their resolution three times. ?][? if e21_masses_stance = 3 : Zetkin goes to Lenin's office with the delegation's mandate, and they talk for two hours. ?][? if e21_masses_stance = 4 : Radek calls the German declaration a declaration of independence, and congratulates the delegates in private. ?] The congress adopts Lenin's theses: the communist parties are to win the majority of the working class before they try to lead it to power.

[? if e21_levi_verdict = 2 : On Levi, the congress censures and does not expel. Lenin's formula is that Levi is to be kept, watched and used, and Zetkin brings him the news herself. ?][? if e21_levi_verdict = 1 : On Levi, the congress decides what the Zentrale would not: he is expelled for breach of discipline. Lenin tells Zetkin afterwards that Levi was right about March, and that he lost his head. ?][? if e21_levi_verdict = 3 : The congress confirms Levi's expulsion. Lenin tells Zetkin privately that Levi was right about March, and had no right to say it the way he did. ?][? if e21_levi_verdict = 3 and e21_levi_plea = 1 : He agrees that the door may open again if Levi submits to the party. Levi has not said he will. ?]

The delegates go home to prepare for the party congress at Jena in August.
